Additional reviewed lexical evidence
------------------------------------

The bundled character-reading forms and selected lexical facts include adapted
material from Japanese and English Wiktionary contributors, licensed under
Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International. Japanese character
forms were extracted by Kaikki/wiktextract. English character forms were
extracted directly from pinned primary MediaWiki page revisions. This project
filters, normalizes, and reviews their applicability. Source titles, original
forms, tags, revision or archive provenance, and modification details are
retained in data/character-readings.json, data/english-character-readings.json,
data/lexical-evidence.json, and sources.lock.json.

The English character bundle uses source version
enwiktionary-api-20261009-6017-pages. Its v2 bundle is 2,528,877 bytes and contains
3,726 records for 3,560 distinct character/reading pairs across 2,243 characters.
Bundle SHA256:
19de3d104423590dbcdc7afa68d4eb53f42727e4c35932532a541d8ecb206670
Primary page snapshot SHA256:
168070d2cfa2da11bed52773cef17bb6fcc71e2d713d845cdeb811b083dc0d1a

The importer retains literal on-readings, explicitly complete kun-readings,
and documented character-reading prefixes. It withholds unmarked kun, nanori,
historical values, and unsupported markup, and infers no sound changes or
inflections. Individual source records preserve exact page revision URLs.

Japanese Wiktionary: https://ja.wiktionary.org/
English Wiktionary: https://en.wiktionary.org/
Extraction: https://kaikki.org/dictionary/rawdata.html
Primary revision API: https://en.wiktionary.org/w/api.php
Template documentation: https://en.wiktionary.org/w/index.php?title=Template:ja-readings/documentation&oldid=89401685
License: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/
Copyright: https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Wiktionary:Copyrights

Reviewed local alignment candidates also originated in Doublevil/JmdictFurigana
release 2.3.1+2026-09-25, whose generated data is distributed under the JMdict
Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike license. Supported lexical units were
selected and adapted after two independent AI reviews; no implementation code
was imported. Individual source URLs, evidence, rationales, and review
provenance are retained in data/lexical-evidence.json. Some moderately supported
units rely on a single lexical source; independent reviews do not imply
independent dictionary corroboration.

Candidate data: https://github.com/Doublevil/JmdictFurigana

